From 3c9d6dcd91dd4d58b7db453f92b29b15a2b02b0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mratan <mattdratan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:53:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] capture: full register-table snapshots + event markers
 (divergence plan)

Implements every row of DIVERGENCE-DEBUG-PLAN.md's 'What a
Pre-firmware capture must record' table as kernel-side reads, emitted
in a normalized field-per-line format (CAPTURE-REG / CAPTURE-PMIC /
CAPTURE-CPUPCR / CAPTURE-EMI) at the plan's sequence points inside the
vendor CONSYS bring-up:

- mtk_wcn_consys_hw.c: wmt_capture_regtable() reads the full table
  (AP-side SPM/INFRA/TOPCKGEN/WDT/pwrap-bridge regs always; CONN-side
  chip-ID/HW_VER/ACR/CPUPCR gated on SPM_PWR_STATUS+2ND bit1, the
  bsg100-H16 DEVAPC lesson; BTIF block gated on CLK_INFRA_BTIF, APDMA
  on CLK_INFRA_AP_DMA; MT6351 VCN LDOs + DCXO_CW00 via exported
  pwrap_read -- the rows devmem cannot reach; CONSYS EMI ctrl-window
  CRC32 + first 64 bytes). wmt_capture_cpupcr_burst() takes the >=32
  samples at ~1ms the plan demands. Hooked at reg_ctrl entry/off,
  pre-chipid-poll, mcu-reset-release (incl. burst -- the exact window
  bsg100 never captured) and after-reg-ctrl-on, plus CAPTURE-MCU-RST
  assert/release event lines at the WDT swsysrst writes.
- wmt_core.c: per-step CAPTURE-INIT start/result lines for every
  init_table_* script step (PASS / TX-FAIL / RX-FAIL / EVT-MISMATCH).
- stp_core.c: CAPTURE-STP-MODE line on every mand<->full transition.
- btif_plat.c: CAPTURE-BTIF-INIT full host-register dump at
  hal_btif_hw_init, CAPTURE-BTIF-FIFO-CLR markers at FIFO clears.

All reads; the only writes are printk. Compiles clean with the period
GCC 6.3 stretch container (banner #1 SMP PREEMPT, symbols verified in
System.map).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
